      "writtenOn": "2026-03-03T11:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The code will still compile because the value is a valid integer, but it will trigger a linter error. For example \n```              \nGPUTextureDescriptor(\n                    size \u003d GPUExtent3D(width \u003d 1),\n                    format \u003d 12121, //Invalid value\n                    usage \u003d TextureUsage.TextureBinding or TextureUsage.CopyDst\n                )\n\n```\n\nThis will prompt a linter warning: \u0027Must be one of: TextureFormat.Undefined, TextureFormat.R8Unorm...\u0027\"",
      "parentUuid": "3acdcdc0_b6bf62d7",
